 "about": "8.2 to 8.5: the Meeting Hub organization CA held by a Standard console. Every ECDSA signature is P-256 SHA-256 with RFC 6979 nonces; a Rust test compares tbs_hex and info_hex and verifies der_hex. Certificates: v3, serial 16 bytes, ecdsa-with-SHA256 without parameters, the CA subject copied as issuer, UTCTime before 2050, extensions basicConstraints (critical), keyUsage (critical), extKeyUsage, subjectAltName in names order (dNSName, then iPAddress, or the URI), subjectKeyIdentifier (first 20 bytes of SHA-256 of the key's point), authorityKeyIdentifier [0] the CA's; server from now - 5 minutes to now + 90 days, signer client to now + 30 days (never past the CA). CRLs: v2, nextUpdate thisUpdate + 120 days, entries by revocation time then serial, revokedCertificates omitted when empty, crlExtensions AKI then cRLNumber. order: the later thisUpdate wins, at equal thisUpdate the higher number when both carry one, else none. reader: current once thisUpdate has passed, pending up to 5 minutes ahead, future beyond. dates: thisUpdate = max(now - 5 minutes, last + 1 s), never after now.",
